org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> CSL FINALIZER ACTUAL org-cite-csl-finalizer
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> PUBLIC org-cite-register-processor "Mark citation processor NAME as available.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> NAME is a symbol.  BODY is a property list, where the following
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> optional keys can be set:
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>   `:activate'
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     Function activating a citation.  It is called with a single
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     argument: a citation object extracted from the current
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     buffer.  It may add text properties to the buffer.  If it is
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     not provided, `org-cite-fontify-default' is used.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>   `:export-bibliography'
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     Function rendering a bibliography.  It is called with six
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     arguments: the list of citation keys used in the document, as
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     strings, a list of bibliography files, the style, as a string
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     or nil, the local properties, as a property list, the export
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     backend, as a symbol, and the communication channel, as a
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     property list.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     It is called at each \"print_bibliography\" keyword in the
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     parse tree.  It may return a string, a parsed element, a list
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     of parsed elements, or nil.  When it returns nil, the keyword
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     is ignored.  Otherwise, the value it returns replaces the
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     keyword in the export output.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>   `:export-citation'    (mandatory for \"export\" capability)
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     Function rendering citations.  It is called with four
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     arguments: a citation object, the style, as a pair, the
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     export backend, as a symbol, and the communication channel,
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     as a property list.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     It is called on each citation object in the parse tree.  It
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     may return a string, a parsed object, a secondary string, or
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     nil.  When it returns nil, the citation is ignored.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     Otherwise, the value it returns replaces the citation object
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     in the export output.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>   `:export-finalizer'
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     Function called at the end of export process.  It must accept
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     six arguments: the output, as a string, a list of citation
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     keys used in the document, a list of bibliography files, the
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     expected bibliography style, as a string or nil, the export
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     backend, as a symbol, and the communication channel, as a
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     property list.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     It must return a string, which will become the final output
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     from the export process, barring subsequent modifications
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     from export filters.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>   `:follow'
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     Function called to follow a citation.  It accepts two
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     arguments, the citation or citation reference object at
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     point, and any prefix argument received during interactive
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     call of `org-open-at-point'.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>   `:insert'
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     Function called to insert a citation.  It accepts two
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     arguments, the citation or citation reference object at point
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     or nil, and any prefix argument received.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>   `:cite-styles'
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     When the processor has export capability, the value can
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     specify what cite styles, variants, and their associated
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     shortcuts are supported.  It can be useful information for
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     completion or linting.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     The expected format is
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>       ((STYLE . SHORTCUTS) . VARIANTS))
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     where STYLE is a string, SHORTCUTS a list of strings or nil,
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     and VARIANTS is a list of pairs (VARIANT . SHORTCUTS),
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     VARIANT being a string and SHORTCUTS a list of strings or
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     nil.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     The \"nil\" style denotes the processor fall-back style.  It
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     should have a corresponding entry in the value.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     The value can also be a function.  It will be called without
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe>     any argument and should return a list structured as the above.
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> 
org-texmacs-standard-cite-probe> Return a non-nil value on a successful operation.
